1
00:00:02,930 --> 00:00:06,770
The Grand Canyon is a unique and spectacular landform.

2
00:00:06,970 --> 00:00:13,450
There is nothing quite like it anywhere else on Earth, but if we cast our gaze to more distant horizons,

3
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:17,230
we can find another similarly amazing location.

4
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:20,770
The planet Mars has its own Grand Canyon,

5
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:26,850
Valles Marineris, and it is interesting to compare Mars' Canyon with ours.

6
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:33,970
The full sweep of the grandeur of Earth's Grand Canyon can be seen very well by looking down from space.

7
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:41,050
Here we see the canyon's winding path stretching from Lake Powell in the east to Lake Mead in the west.

8
00:00:42,370 --> 00:00:45,530
Similarly, in this view from NASA's Viking orbiter,

9
00:00:45,730 --> 00:00:51,170
we can see Valles Marineris reaching across vast stretches of the Martian terrain.

10
00:00:51,850 --> 00:00:56,890
Earth's Grand Canyon is actually a large network of interconnecting canyons.

11
00:00:57,490 --> 00:01:03,180
The same can be said for Valles Marineris on Mars.

12
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:08,580
The deep cut and steep walls of the Grand Canyon

13
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:14,420
expose many layers of geological deposits, reaching way back into time.

14
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:18,700
Similarly, Valles Marineris displays numerous layers,

15
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:25,140
including lake floor sedimentary deposits, laid down in Mars' distant watery past.

16
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:33,560
The deep cut made by the Colorado River has been significantly widened by numerous landslides

17
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:36,240
along the Grand Canyon's steep walls.

18
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:43,840
Surprise Valley is nearly filled with debris from the largest landslide deposit in the Grand Canyon,

19
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,920
containing over a cubic mile of displaced material.

20
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:54,480
Nearby, Deer Creek is cutting a new gorge as it bypasses landslide blockage.

21
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:59,520
Zooming down toward Eus Lobis in Valles Marineris,

22
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:04,960
we see a Titanic landslide deposit measuring over 30 miles across

23
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:09,040
and stretching 25 miles out across the floor of the valley.

24
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:12,600
In places along the northwestern edge of the Grand Canyon,

25
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:18,760
we find volcanic cinder cones from which flows of lava cascaded over the canyon walls

26
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:21,320
into the gorge of the Colorado River.

27
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:28,520
These flows built temporary dams that created lakes that partially filled the canyon in its past.

28
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:33,960
To the northwest of Valles Marineris, we also find volcanoes,

29
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:40,640
the giant Tharsus Shield Volcanoes, which played key roles in the formation of the canyon.

30
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:46,720
These mountains include Olympus Mons, the greatest volcano in the solar system,

31
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:53,280
standing three times the height of Mount Everest and with a base 370 miles across.

32
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:59,040
Flowing Water played a critical role in the Grand Canyon's formation

33
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:02,320
with the Colorado River cutting the canyon's deep gorge.

34
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:06,880
Flowing Water also played a role in Valles Marineris.

35
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:14,960
This color-coded height map shows where channels of water float out of the canyon into a great bay.

36
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:22,080
While they have many similarities, the two canyons also have significant differences.

37
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:28,960
The Grand Canyon was formed primarily by erosion through the cutting power of the Colorado River.

38
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:32,880
While Water altered the landscape of Valles Marineris,

39
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:36,880
this feature is far too big to have been cut by water.

40
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:41,040
It is a great tectonic fracture of the planet's crust.

41
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,040
Size is another key difference between the two canyons.

42
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:52,560
Valles Marineris is far larger. If it were on Earth, it could stretch from the US's east coast

43
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:59,200
to west coast, with many of its smaller sub-canyons still dwarfing our Grand Canyon.

44
00:04:03,570 --> 00:04:09,810
Another difference is that Earth's Grand Canyon now hosts over 6 million visitors per year.

45
00:04:10,930 --> 00:04:17,170
Valles Marineris is still waiting to receive its first tourists. Perhaps you will be one of them.

